usage: neuraxis [-h]
                {fetch-models,validate-models,run-reference,calibrate-tolerances,generate-mutants,classify-mutants,build-fingerprints,select-protocols,evaluate-heldout,evaluate-agent,analyze,reproduce-paper,pilot,smoke,curate-models,smoke-test}
                ...

Neuraxis command-line interface (spec "Suggested commands"). Every command is
a thin wrapper around ``neuraxis.experiments``. Commands never touch held-out
data except ``evaluate-heldout``, which is gated by ``configs/FROZEN.lock``.

positional arguments:
  {fetch-models,validate-models,run-reference,calibrate-tolerances,generate-mutants,classify-mutants,build-fingerprints,select-protocols,evaluate-heldout,evaluate-agent,analyze,reproduce-paper,pilot,smoke,curate-models,smoke-test}
    fetch-models        download commit-pinned model snapshots with provenance
    validate-models     structural validation of manifest models
    run-reference       reference fingerprints at h, h/2, h/4 + determinism
    calibrate-tolerances
                        tolerance table from reference refinement
    generate-mutants    mutants and valid transformations
    classify-mutants    fingerprint, compare and classify generated variants
    build-fingerprints  fingerprint, compare and classify generated variants
    select-protocols    greedy selection + random baselines on the discovery
                        split
    evaluate-heldout    GATED held-out evaluation (requires
                        configs/FROZEN.lock)
    evaluate-agent      score one agent trial with hidden deterministic
                        evaluators
    analyze             metrics, statistics and figures from processed results
    reproduce-paper     rebuild all tables and figures from raw/processed
                        results
    pilot               run the Milestone 6 pilot end to end
    smoke               quick end-to-end simulator smoke check
    curate-models       apply the model inclusion/exclusion criteria
                        (reference simulations only)
    smoke-test          infrastructure smoke test (the execution plan's nine
                        checks)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit

